# Receipt — sub-spec 07-posixshfix (change optimize-test-suite)
# Session outcome. Suite touched: tests/installsh-posixsh_test.sh. The root
# red posixsh-04 is fixed era-independently and keeps its id: the pair of
# base-vs-working render registrations (HOME-tree diff -r plus the console
# report whose grep -vxF subtraction fed a `printf '%s\n' "$added" | grep -c
# ''` count — the empty-removal "got: 1" bug) is re-keyed to ONE
# console-inventory registration: a single fresh hermetic --all render of the
# CURRENT install.sh through the harness library's render helper (the suite
# now sources tests/harness.sh and defines none of its helpers itself),
# asserted whole-report and in order by cmp against the documented 22-line
# inventory (2 client status + 4 script-artifact report + 12 client
# "Installed" + 4 libdir "Installed"; inventory verified on disk against the
# actual fresh render; only the version token normalized, every other byte
# pinned). The tree-identity registration is gone (its sixteen-file tree is
# pinned by the render and libdir suites; posixsh-04's 16 "Installed" lines
# keep the report-side shape). The base-extraction machinery
# (base_install_sh, prep_base_if_distinct, base_install_file, the local
# render_tree copy, every merge-base/show-HEAD:/$base-era clause) is deleted;
# posixsh-01 keeps its synthetic three-hit pin and drops the historical
# clause; posixsh-02's negative control is carried by the synthetic trap
# fixture alone; posixsh-03's two registrations are byte-identical to before
# ("otherwise unchanged", with the base clauses excised from 01/02). Four
# id-tagged posixshfix tests guard the re-key over the suite's own
# (comment-stripped) source with quote-split needles so no forbidden literal
# is self-carried. Session-sensitivity checks: a report mutation (client
# label "Claude Code" -> "ClaudeX Code") turned posixsh-04 and posixshfix-01
# red with exact expected-vs-actual dumps (install.sh then restored
# byte-identical); a re-injected legacy_probe/base_install_sh helper plus a
# re-added `grep -c ''` idiom turned posixshfix-01/-02/-04 red while
# posixshfix-03 and posixsh-04 correctly stayed green. Deviations resolved:
# (1) "keeps its name" read as keeping the posixsh-04 id at the start of the
# reported name; the tail reworded to the new console-inventory behavior
# since the old tails described the deleted diff semantics; (2) posixsh-03's
# env -i no-flag refusal run keeps its direct invocation — it is an
# execution/refusal check whose sanitized PATH is not expressible through
# install_at, not a "render" in the Background's sense; (3) the version
# token stays free so the expectation derives from the inventory plus the
# current install.sh's own output alone (no VERSION read); (4) the
# "exits 0, every id green" clause is bought by the recorded runs below,
# never a self-recursive suite execution (permanent law 1). Product surfaces
# (agents/, install.sh, scripts/orchestration/, spdd/specs/) and spdd/archive/
# untouched. Suite: sh tests/installsh-posixsh_test.sh -> pass=9 fail=0
# skip=0 exit 0 (was pass=5 fail=1 skip=0 exit 1 at session start with the
# posixsh-04 console "got: 1" red; the four posixshfix tests were
# red-verified against the old shape first). Runner: sh tests/run_all.sh ->
# suites=31 passed=31 failed=0 tests_failed=0 (posixsh suite line: pass=9
# fail=0 skip=0 -> ok); elapsed 86s, above the README's 60s target — an
# area-wide budget concern owned by the runner/e2e-QA scope, not this
# sub-spec (this suite contributes 1.7s).
test_command=sh tests/installsh-posixsh_test.sh
id=posixshfix-01 result=green reason=unit test "posixshfix-01: posixsh-04's console half asserts the fresh render against the documented inventory and order, from the current install.sh alone, with no second render and no comparison-derived line count" (extracts posixsh_04's own-source body: exactly one harness render-helper line, referencing INSTALL_SH; embedded inventory anchors at head, script-report tail, and libdir tail; whole-report cmp -s; body and suite refuse the comparison machinery and both counting idioms; then runs the clause itself green at the current disk state)
id=posixshfix-02 result=green reason=unit test "posixshfix-02: the base-extraction machinery and the tree-identity registration are gone; every render uses the current install.sh; posixsh-01..03 keep their ids, registrations, and synthetic instruments" (whole-suite non-comment scan: base_install_sh/base_install_file/prep_base_if_distinct/$base/merge-base byte-identical pre-fix-render all refused; harness sourced, zero locally defined library helpers; posixsh_01 body keeps write_trap_fixture + the -eq 3 pin and refuses base; posixsh_02 body keeps the trap-fixture negative control and refuses base and the historical line-230 error pin; registrations posixsh-01:1 -02:1 -03:2)
id=posixshfix-03 result=green reason=unit test "posixshfix-03: the retained posixsh-04 id keeps its name with exactly one console-inventory registration, and all nine scenario registrations are accounted for" (exactly one run_test line headed "posixsh-04 ", matching *console*posixsh_04; nine id-headed registrations total; posixshfix-01..04 one each; the scenario's exits-0-every-id-green line is bought by the recorded runs — suite pass=9 fail=0 skip=0 exit 0 and runner 31/31 — never a self-recursive suite execution, per permanent law 1)
id=posixshfix-04 result=green reason=unit test "posixshfix-04: the retained suite source holds no history comparison, no byte-pin against the default branch, and no exact-phrase pin of prompts or docs" (whole-suite non-comment scan refuses every history literal — git, HEAD, merge-base, git show, show HEAD:, diff --quiet, diff - , base_commit: — and every prompt/docs prose-pin reference — agents/prompts, agents/meta, .prompt, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, spdd/; assertions on install.sh's own output and the installed product-file paths in the inventory are the sub-spec's explicit non-pins)
